From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:47:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 092/117] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali: list the MDP SS IP clock
 for the DPU

The display controller is also clocked by DISP_CC_MDSS_MDP_SS_IP_CLK (the
stock device tree passes it to the MDP as its SS IP clock), but the DPU
node does not list it, so Linux never votes for it and the controller
only works when the boot loader happened to leave it running. When it
did not, boots can scan out a correct top band followed by stale data.

Add the clock to the DPU clocks so the DPU enables it with the others
(the driver takes all listed clocks as a bulk set).

Found by Reixo0 on the RedMagic 11 Pro (SM8850), in github Reixo0/linux
commit 8b4f66b1d043 ("arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali: give the display controller its SS IP clock")
(no Signed-off-by); this one-line change is written independently from
the stock device tree's MDP clock list.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
index 39667f09a19aa..e02d58a1bd3c6 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
@@ -4609,12 +4609,14 @@ mdss_mdp: display-controller@9801000 {
 					 <&dispcc DISP_CC_MDSS_AHB_CLK>,
 					 <&dispcc DISP_CC_MDSS_MDP_LUT_CLK>,
 					 <&dispcc DISP_CC_MDSS_MDP_CLK>,
-					 <&dispcc DISP_CC_MDSS_VSYNC_CLK>;
+					 <&dispcc DISP_CC_MDSS_VSYNC_CLK>,
+					 <&dispcc DISP_CC_MDSS_MDP_SS_IP_CLK>;
 				clock-names = "nrt_bus",
 					      "iface",
 					      "lut",
 					      "core",
-					      "vsync";
+					      "vsync",
+					      "ssip";
 
 				assigned-clocks = <&dispcc DISP_CC_MDSS_VSYNC_CLK>;
 				assigned-clock-rates = <19200000>;
